6. Components the user installs, which citegeist only calls
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Claude Code, Codex CLI and Cursor CLI run as the user's own installations under the user's own
  accounts and terms. citegeist starts them through the Agent Client Protocol adapters
  @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp and @agentclientprotocol/codex-acp (Apache-2.0).
  The adapter for Claude Code depends on @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk, which is published under
  Anthropic's legal agreements (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance) and not
  under an open source license.
  Zotero Connector: the user's browser extension, AGPL-3.0, talks to citegeist over the Connector
  protocol. citegeist contains no Zotero code. "Zotero" is a trademark of the Corporation for
  Digital Scholarship.

